From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:48:54 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/tests: test the stereo modes of detailed timings and
 DisplayID

Three sinks that declare stereo outside the HDMI VSDB, made by a script
and checked with edid-decode (all three pass --check):
- stereo flags in four detailed timings (E-EDID 1.4, Table 3.22): 1080p60
  field sequential with the right image on sync 1, the first timing,
  720p60 field sequential with the left image on sync 1, 1080i60 field
  sequential and 1024x768@60 2-way interleaved. Every timing keeps its 2D
  mode, the first preferred; the two progressive field sequential ones
  are also listed frame sequential, never preferred, with their 1000/1001
  twins, and the interlaced and the interleaved ones are not;
- a DisplayID 2.0 extension with a Type VII timing that reports 3D, one
  that does not, and a Stereo Display Interface block (0x27) for field
  sequential over the timings reporting 3D and the codes DMT 0x55, VIC 16
  and HDMI VIC 1: four frame-sequential modes, none for the mono-only
  timing, and both 2D modes kept;
- a DisplayID 1.3 extension with two Type I timings that report no 3D and
  two Stereo Display Interface blocks (0x10) over all listed timings, one
  field sequential, one side by side: both timings frame sequential, and
  no side by side mode yet.

The expected modes are those edid-decode prints for the three EDIDs,
with DRM's own rules (no stereo copy of interlaced timings, 1000/1001
twins of 60 Hz CTA-861 formats).

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/tests/drm_edid_3d_test.c | 249 ++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 246 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

